    "success_criteria": {
      "criteria": [
        "A measure/v1 payload that carries producer_version and accounting_basis (agent-cost 0.2.0) is accepted by the telemetry adapter and both values are persisted on the cost_ledger entry that usage-import or calibrate writes; a payload without them (agent-cost 0.1.x) persists accounting_basis \"unknown\" explicitly rather than omitting the field.",
        "eligible_for_knn is false and the entry records an estimate/v2 reason code when any of these holds for the measurement behind it: TOKEN_BASIS_MISMATCH when accounting_basis is not the current basis (agent-cost-raw-total/v2); MIXED_OR_UNATTRIBUTED_USAGE when data_quality.conflicting_duplicate_groups > 0, data_quality.missing_dedup_identity_rows > 0, data_quality.source_quality.identity_missing > 0, or any session_id of the entry is not exactly_attributed under attribution/v1 (unbound, orphan, or bound to more than one task_run); the existing matched-and-fully-priced condition still applies on top.",
        "Re-measuring a lane whose existing cost_ledger entry was produced under a different accounting_basis never silently overwrites that entry: computeLedgerEntryId keeps its (lane, phase, source, pricing_version) parity identity unchanged, the basis mismatch is detected, and the new measurement is written as a superseding entry with both bases visible (or refused with a diagnostic naming both bases), asserted by a test that fails against the pre-change code.",
        "Every reason that made an entry ineligible is visible in the entry itself and in the calibration observation as an estimate/v2 reason code plus a fixed-template detail string (spec.md T-1..T-11), and the estimate/v2 abstain output shows the reason code for that candidate; the estimate/v2 contract itself is not versioned up, and nothing about the reason lives only in stderr.",
        "The existing packages/* test suites stay green, measure/v1 fixtures without the new fields still validate, and no new required field is added to the measure/v1 payload contract."
      ],
      "recorded_at": "2026-09-14T18:36:24.171Z"
    }
  }
